      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2011 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "A novel series of 4-arylphthalazin-1(2H)-one linked to arylpiperidines were synthesized and evaluated as MCH-R1 antagonists. The results of an extensive SAR study probing the effects of substituents on the 4-arylphthalazin-1(2H)-one C-4 aryl group led to the identification of the 4-(3,4-difluorophenyl) derivative as a highly potent MCH-R1 inhibitor with an IC(50)=1nM. However, further investigations showed that this substance has unacceptable pharmacokinetic properties including a high clearance and volume of distribution."
      },
